A glob view prints a YAML file's header comment, or else a field summary of its first three scalar keys, with `...` when more follow; a file with only mappings and lists prints its keys' names instead.
== args
input
== file input/commented.yaml
# Commented settings.
a: 1
== file input/compose.yml
version: "3"
services:
  web: {}
name: demo
== file input/many.yaml
a: 1
b: two
c: true
d: null
== file input/nested.yaml
a:
  b: 1
== stdout
glob view: input
input/commented.yaml (2 lines): Commented settings.
input/compose.yml (4 lines): {version: "3", name: demo}
input/many.yaml (4 lines): {a: 1, b: two, c: true, ...}
input/nested.yaml (2 lines): {a}
== stderr
== exit 0
